  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">FAS 2013-2015</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FAS, Femmes Africa Solidarit&#xe9; 2013-2015 - FAS 2013-2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An international women&#x2019;s organization working to empower African      women to assume a leadership role in peace building and conflict      resolution. It supports activities promoting peace and security in    Africa with a gender perspective. Main pillars advocacy and           empowerment.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">En internationell kvinnoorganisation som arbetar f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka       afrikanska kvinnor s&#xe5; att de ska kunna anta ledande roller inom       fredbyggande och konfliktl&#xf6;sning. FAS st&#xf6;djer fredfr&#xe4;mjande och       s&#xe4;kerhetsrelaterade aktiviteter med ett genusperspektiv. huvudaxlar   p&#xe5;verkansarbete och empowerment/st&#xe4;rkande av gr&#xe4;srotsorganisationer.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vision: The overall orientation and underlying meaning of FAS interventions lie in the following vision: A prosperous African continent with women participating actively as key players in all aspects of peace and security processes.Mission: In order to contribute to this vision of the &#x201c;reality to be&#x201d;, FAS reason to exist is to &#x201c;Mobilize the power of women to forge peace and drive prosperity in Africa&#x201d; along with the core values of solidarity, inclusiveness, commitment and accountability.
FAS&apos; areas of intervention included: policy advocacy and capacity building in conflict and post-conflict managemement, conflict prevention, with a focus on women&apos;s participation, and implementation of UNSC Res. 1325 on Women, Peace and Security. The organization had close cooperation with AU, ECOWAS and the UN.</narrative>
  </description>
